NOTE ON EMPTY-STATE FIDELITY (Honesty Covenant #9 — documented, not silent)
  The web page never gates its whole body: it always renders the summary card (zeros), hides the
  comparison chart below 2 routes, renders no route cards, and shows the Route-Metrics EmptyState.
  The native surface keeps that contract — loading/error are the only full-body switches; otherwise
  the body renders, the comparison ChartContainer shows its Empty surface (<2 routes), the route-cards
  region is omitted (web renders none), and the Route-Metrics panel shows its EmptyState. So the
  declared `empty` data state is genuinely reachable via two empty-state composables, never a blank
  region. AI route-efficiency suggestions (web AIRouteEfficiencySuggestions) are a separate, withAiFeature
  -gated parity unit and out of scope here (no panel/string for it in this manifest record).

